      {
        "title": "Show HN: Corgi, a helpful {agent, terminal} multiplexer",
        "link": "https://corgi.computer/",
        "description": "<p>Hey everyone,<p>Inspired by Herdr, I've built an agent multiplexer that I've been using as my daily driver for a few weeks now.<p>I think I improved on the concept in a few ways, focusing on the ergonomics I always wished I had:<p>I show you what the agents are up to, along with a running feed of their activity.\nThere's also a simple shortcut (F1) to go to the next unread agent.<p>I use multiple accounts, so I've added unified launcher for Codex/Claude Code/Pi.\nTheres some careful ergonomics there: fast search and resume over sessions, inline usage tracking etc.<p>Many small quality of life improvements to the terminal experience:\n- Links can be copied with a click, so no need to drag-select over many lines\n- cmd+v just pastes images (even on SSH)\n- images have a thumbnail preview.\n- Built-in CPU/Memory/GPU usage tracking, broken down by workspace<p>I assume you have access to cheap inference (Luna/Haiku/etc).\nIt just reuses the agents to organize things for you: what is this http link? what is this worktree about? what is each agent doing? \nIt's small but it made my environment feel more cozy.<p>On a personal note, I've been on a frustrating sick leave for a while now.\nI created Corgi to challenge myself, and see if I can go back.\nThe answer is more mixed than I had hoped, but I am happy with the result and thankful for the experience.<p>I hope you like it! a few friends & myself have been using it for a few weeks and it's been pretty nice.\nThere's still a lot to improve and some rough edges, so feedback would be greatly appreciated.<p>Thank you :)</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50214373\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50214373</a></p>\n<p>Points: 51</p>\n<p># Comments: 10</p>",
        "pubDate": "Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:46:38 +0000",
        "guid": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50214373"
      },
